### Are there known steps to reproduce?

_No response_

### How are you running AnythingLLM?

Docker (local)

### What happened?

The Agent query and response history from the 'default' thread spill over into newly created threads. 

Steps:
- Do an agent based web-search query in the default thread of your workspace. 
- Close the agent session
- Open new thread
- Do a new agent call in this thread that has no previous messages in it
- See a response that is referring to info from the previous thread 

Default thread:
![image](https://github.com/Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm/assets/6628064/1ad4fbf1-2135-49dc-94aa-612c8fbcb87f)

New thread:
![image](https://github.com/Mintplex-Labs/anything-llm/assets/6628064/1ee749ab-0899-4e9d-ab36-3b553b0b17a1)

logs of first message in new thread look normal:
```json
[2024-05-10 23:01:08.203] [INFO] Received POST request to /v1/chat/completions with body: {
  "model": "lmstudio-community/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct-BPE-fix-GGUF/Meta-Llama-3-8B-Instruct-Q8_0.gguf",
  "stream": true,
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "You are a smart, precise and helpful AI assistant. Use the provided context to answer the user's questions. Do not make up answers that are not in the context.
"
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "This is text in a new thread"
    }
  ],
  "temperature": 0.7
}
```

The first agent call does not
